## Summary

Finding every file or folder tagged with an xattr today means walking the
whole tree and asking each entry, which is why nobody builds on xattrs.
Make the filesystem answer like a database instead: an index, maintained
incrementally from filesystem events, that answers "everything with
attribute X" in query time rather than traversal time.

## Prior art

flecs: entities with components, queried by component. Files are entities,
xattrs are components; the same query model applies.

Drafted by Claude Code (Fable); comments wanted, hence the RFC flag.
